  "lastAssistantText": "Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n**Defect:** In `saveHistory()`, after `history.push(imageData)` the `historyIndex` was never advanced to point at the newly saved frame. Since the initial `historyIndex = -1` and no increment occurred, subsequent calls left `historyIndex` frozen at `0`. This made undo a NO-OP (because `undo()` checks `if (historyIndex <= 0)` and `historyIndex` stayed at `0`) and caused the status bar to report wrong counts (`1/2`, `1/2` instead of `1/1`, `2/2`).\n\n**Fix:** Added `historyIndex = history.length;` immediately before `history.push(imageData)`. This sets the index to point at the new last element (since `push` appends at position `length`, and after the push, that element is at index `length - 1`... wait \u2014 let me double-check one more time).\n\nActually, re-examining: `historyIndex = history.length` is set *before* the push. If `history.length` was 2 (indices 0,1), then `historyIndex = 2`, and after `push()` the array has 3 elements at indices 0, 1, **2** \u2014 which matches! \u2705\n\nAfter any trimming by the `shift()` loop, the index is adjusted down accordingly. The fallback branch handles edge cases where the index might still land on an invalid position.",
