        "number": 1,
        "id": "feedback1-1795004093-343",
        "message": "DEFECT: undo/redo history index never advances after saving a new state (undo is effectively broken).\n\nEVIDENCE (behavioral, run in a Node vm against the shipped artifact .observed/current/index.html, hash verified 2fc29e49...04705d7):\n- Page loads with no runtime errors; palette, canvas, and all toolbar handlers wire up.\n- Simulate a single action (btn \"Clear\" runs clearCanvas(true) + saveHistory()).\n- After the 1st action the status bar shows \"History: 1/2\" instead of 1/1.\n- After the 2nd action it still shows \"History: 1/2\" instead of 2/3.\n- Pressing Undo leaves the status unchanged (\"History: 1/2\") -> Undo is a NO-OP.\n- Redo then jumps to \"History: 2/2\".\n\nROOT CAUSE (in saveHistory(), index ~line 873 of index.html):\n  history.push(imageData);\n  while (history.length > MAX_HISTORY) { history.shift(); ... }\n  if (!history[historyIndex]) { historyIndex = history.length > 0 ? history.length - 1 : -1; }\nThe push grows the array but historyIndex is NEVER incremented to point at the newly saved frame. history[oldIndex] still exists, so the correction branch never fires. Only the very first saveHistory (starting historyIndex=-1) lands correctly via the fallback. From the 2nd action on, the index is frozen.\n\nEXPECTED OUTCOME:\n- historyIndex must be set to history.length - 1 immediately after push (the new frame IS the current state).\n- After any single action the counter should be 1/1 (first) then 2/2 (second), etc.\n- Undo must revert the just-performed action; it must NOT be a no-op after an action.\n- Redo must be disabled at the top of history; undo disabled only at the oldest frame.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS: undo/redo is a required feature of the brief and is currently broken for the normal case (draw an action, then undo does nothing). The status counter is also wrong.\n\nNOTE (preserve good behavior): brush/eraser stroke rendering, Bresenham line drawing, coordinate scaling under zoom, touch handlers, and PNG export (dataURL generation + anchor click) all behave correctly and should NOT be changed. This is the one functional defect found so far.\n",
        "reason": "Verified via Node-vm simulation against hash-verified artifact: saveHistory() never increments historyIndex after push, making Undo a no-op and the history counter wrong. Requires a fix to the undo/redo stack.",
